# Release criteria for v0.1, as plan section 9 states them.
#
# These are TARGETS, not measurements — the plan says so in as many words,
# and this file is committed before any hardware number exists precisely so
# that it cannot be adjusted to fit one later. A criterion changed after a
# run must be changed in a commit of its own, with a reason.
#
# Only what the plan quantifies is here. The plan also asks for a hardware
# profile to be fixed after the first feasibility run and for thresholds to
# be frozen before the final test; criteria that need that profile (memory
# growth rate, power draw) arrive then, as their own reviewed change, rather
# than being invented now to look complete.
version 1
profile v0.1

require peak_rss_bytes                 <=  1610612736   whole-process peak, 1.5 GiB, no swap
require observation_p95_ms             <=  10000        per semantic observation at the fixed image/ROI profile
require package_event_latency_p95_ms   <=  45000        from first visible placement in ground truth, confirmation included
require package_precision              >=  0.95         on held-out scenes
require package_recall                 >=  0.90         on held-out scenes
require false_package_events_per_24h   <=  1            negative continuous run
require door_earliest_event_s          >=  300          no door event before 300 s of valid evidence
require uptime_hours                   >=  24           no crash, no unbounded queue
require offline_operation              >=  1            1 when fully functional with networking disabled
